mation is only half the battle. You must interpret a growing flood of incomplete, conflicting, and sometimes unreliable reports. Is a lead worth sending a field reporter to investigate? Is a story verified enough to air? Are you informing the public, or pushing the town closer to panic?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4910010/extras/f81ea77d486284f6cc112a1df7020637.poster.avif?t=1785932483\" width=780 height=300 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4910010/extras/f81ea77d486284f6cc112a1df7020637.webm?t=1785932483\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4910010/extras/f81ea77d486284f6cc112a1df7020637.mp4?t=1785932483\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >By deciding what information to broadcast, you alone influence how the public responds to the crisis. With the fate of the town on the line, every choice matters. What you air, what you hold back, and what you get wrong can shape the night in ways you may not be able to undo.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4910010/extras/42bb2132af1f380f49b175c24dc16a48.poster.avif?t=1785932483\" width=780 height=300 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4910010/extras/42bb2132af1f380f49b175c24dc16a48.webm?t=1785932483\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4910010/extras/42bb2132af1f380f49b175c24dc16a48.mp4?t=1785932483\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features:</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\